from pathlib import Path
import json,re,hashlib,datetime
r=Path('/Users/jaheba/p/tis/benchmarks/results/overnight-json-bisect-csv');label='final20'
data={mode:{runtime:json.loads((r/label/mode/(runtime+'.json')).read_text())['benchmarks'] for runtime in ['monty','tis-bytecode','tis-native','cpython']} for mode in ['one-shot','repeated']}
names=sorted(data['one-shot']['monty'])
rows=['# Overnight results — 30 October 2026','', 'The overall performance goals were **not achieved**. All 14 full-size selected programs run unchanged with exact CPython stdout. Results use the final validated candidate20; no commits or pushes.','', 'Serial Flying Circus `--quick`, overridden to 12 timing samples per runtime/workload/mode, 1 separate RSS sample and 1 repeated warmup. One-shot means first request in a fresh worker; repeated means fresh VM/session in a reused worker. Both include frontend, tier compilation, execution and output delivery, exclude process startup/reset. Ratios are medians; borderline results remain noisy.','', '| Workload | BC/Monty one / repeated | Native-mode/CPython one / repeated | RSS BC / native MiB |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
passes=[0,0];results={}
for name in names:
 ratios=[]
 for a,b in [('tis-bytecode','monty'),('tis-native','cpython')]:
  ratios.append([data[mode][a][name]['median_wall_seconds']/data[mode][b][name]['median_wall_seconds'] for mode in ['one-shot','repeated']])
 rss=[data['one-shot'][t][name]['median_peak_rss_bytes']/1048576 for t in ['tis-bytecode','tis-native']]
 rows.append(f'| {name} | {ratios[0][0]:.2f} / {ratios[0][1]:.2f} | {ratios[1][0]:.2f} / {ratios[1][1]:.2f} | {rss[0]:.1f} / {rss[1]:.1f} |')
 passes[0]+=all(x<=1.10 for x in ratios[0]);passes[1]+=all(x<1.00 for x in ratios[1]);results[name]={'bytecode_monty':ratios[0],'native_cpython':ratios[1],'rss_bc_native_mib':rss}
rows+=['',f'At the measured medians, {passes[0]}/14 workloads meet bytecode ≤1.10×Monty in both modes; {passes[1]}/14 meet native-mode <CPython in both modes. These are per-workload goals, not an averaged score. RSS is a single whole-process peak sample. Full reports include all four runtimes’ absolute elapsed time and RSS.','', '## Compilation and retained VM measurements','', 'The following retained-VM results are a separate boundary: one compiled Program/VM, globals and caches retained, first execution + 3 warmups + 3 timed executions, exact output checked for all 7 executions. Timings capture output but exclude delivery/frontend. They must not be compared directly to fresh-session CPython. Compile costs are diagnostic runs rather than values subtracted from elapsed time.','', '| Workload | Frontend ms | Bytecode compile ms | First native compile ms | Retained BC / native execution ms | Native entries in diagnostic |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
ret=json.loads((r/'candidate20-retained/results.json').read_text())['rows'];ret={(Path(x['source']).stem,x['tier']):x for x in ret}
diag={x['name']:x['stats'] for x in json.loads((r/'candidate20-diagnostics.json').read_text())}
for name in names:
 bc=ret[name,'bytecode'];native=ret[name,'native'];s=diag[name]
 rows.append(f"| {name} | {native['frontend_ns']/1e6:.3f} | {s.get('bytecode_compile_ns',0)/1e6:.3f} | {s.get('native_compile_ns',0)/1e6:.3f} | {bc['retained_median_ns']/1e6:.3f} / {native['retained_median_ns']/1e6:.3f} | {s.get('native_entries',0)+s.get('native_osr_entries',0)} |")
rows+=['','Native mode includes runtime kernels and interpreter fallback. In particular JSON loads/parse can have zero native entries/compilation; their gains do not establish machine-code speed.','', '## Changes and validation','', '- Added minimal real bisect, lazy generator expressions, raise/basic exceptions and restricted try/except support needed by the unchanged workloads. Multi-clause/async generators, general yield, multi-statement try bodies, finally and except-as remain unsupported; this is not a complete Python stdlib.','- Direct jiter-to-VM JSON decoding, compatible dumps options, owned compact string dictionary keys and hashed sets remove intermediary allocations/quadratic lookups. Borrowed dictionary lookups retain keyed hashes.','- HIR remains central: exact-list append proofs shared across tiers, guarded straight-line generator expression kernels, lazy reusable function bytecode, cached internal try bodies, immediate inline string constants/equality, cheaper dominance/liveness analysis. Profiling windows, GC roots, fallback and deoptimization remain explicit.','- Native inline-string comparisons, IsDone and guarded string iteration reduce runtime/root synchronization. Generator runtime-kernel wins are labeled separately from generated native code.','- Rejected the final dead-constant-elimination experiment after measured JSON regressions; it is not installed. Original Monty and Flying Circus implementations were not edited.','', '[Full final report](final20/report.html) · [Quick comparison](candidate20/report.html) · [Progress, profiling and rejected experiments](PROGRESS.md) · [Frozen binaries and build provenance](candidate20-build-provenance.json) · [Complete final source hashes](candidate20-all-source-sha256.json)','']
count=sum(map(int,re.findall(r'test result: ok\. (\d+) passed',(r/'candidate20-tests.log').read_text())))
reg=json.loads((r/'candidate20-regressions.json').read_text())
rows += [f'Validation: cargo fmt, all-target Clippy with warnings denied, and {count} passing tests. All 14 outputs matched CPython; retained-VM 28 tier/workload rows passed. Fresh-process n-body, Barnes–Hut and unpacking matched pre-overnight output in both tiers. Short single-run regression timings below are directional, not significance claims.','', '| Regression | Tier | Before / final ms |','| --- | --- | ---: |']
for x in reg:rows.append(f"| {x['name']} | {x['tier']} | {x['before_ms']:.1f} / {x['after_ms']:.1f} |")
rows+=['', 'Remaining bottlenecks: CSV still makes millions of generic runtime calls and GC-root synchronizations; native startup compilation dominates small inputs. Bisect still pays Python-loop/tier overhead around fast Rust searches. JSON transforms/lines retain callback and object traffic. Future work should target these measured costs before claiming parity with CPython/PyPy.','']
(r/'FINAL.md').write_text('\n'.join(rows));(r/'LATEST.md').write_text('\n'.join(rows[:rows.index('## Compilation and retained VM measurements')])+ '\n[Full results and validation](FINAL.md)\n')
(r/'final-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps({'generated_utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'target_pass_counts_both_modes':passes,'workloads':results,'tests_passed':count},indent=2)+'\n')
print('\n'.join(rows[:rows.index('## Compilation and retained VM measurements')]))
